  "title": "When to use expected move and when delta is enough",
  "summary": "For covered call strikes or directional bets, delta is enough: a 1-standard-deviation strike on a $100 stock is near $110, about a 16 delta. Use expected move in two cases: earnings trades, where the ATM straddle price gives the move, and range trades like iron condors, where it helps set strikes. Never sell naked options or a naked straddle.",
